# =========================================================================
# CONFIDENTIALITY — these entries are not housekeeping.
#
# The legacy material in this working directory names the pilot host's
# employer and job title. Per CLAUDE.md that must never appear in this
# repository, in commit messages, in issues, or in any generated document.
# These files stay on local disk as the provenance record; they do not go
# into version control.
#
# Do not remove an entry from this block without an explicit decision.
# =========================================================================
field/
private/
data/real/
legacy_notebooks/
legacy_methods/
*.pptx
CoreField_Transformer_Package_*.zip
AUDIT.md
MANIFEST.md

# Internal working instructions. Excluded not because it names anyone -- it
# does not -- but because it states that a confidential pilot exists and that
# identifying detail was removed. Published alongside a founder location, that
# is a pointer to the party being protected. Keep it local.
CLAUDE.md

# The pre-commit hook's term list. Gitignored on purpose: a committed list of
# terms-to-exclude would publish the very terms it protects. See
# scripts/install_hooks.py.
.confidential-terms
*.pre-corefield.bak

# Real telemetry never enters the repo. Templates are the one exception:
# a blank column header file is what a utility engineer gets handed.
*.csv
!**/templates/*.csv
!**/*_template.csv

